  "title": "NASA space satellite images from 2020 and today provide a grim look a...",
  "description": "NASA space satellite images from 2020 and today provide a grim look at how the severely receding Colorado River is affecting Lake Mead. Water levels have been falling for years because of increased demand from farms and cities, hotter temperatures caused by climate change and less snowmelt in the spring. On Tuesday, the federal government announced more restrictions on how much water Arizona and Nevada pull from the river, which serves 40 million people in the American West and Mexico. #lakemead #lakemeaddrought #coloradoriver #climatechange #drought #lakemeadnationalpark #pbs #newshour #pbsnews #pbsnewshour #news #waterrestrictions #arizonawater #nevada #nasa #nasaspace #sattelite #risingtemperature",
